      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "research-evidence-panel",
      "description": "Actual empty evidence state, without invented source rows.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-evidence-panel\"><header><h2>Documentation found</h2></header><div><h3>The evidence will appear here.</h3><p>Start a real research request to see the returned source titles, domains, and links.</p></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-evidence-panel{font-family:\"DM Sans Variable\",sans-serif;min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--border,#272b36);border-radius:11px;background:var(--surface,#13161e);overflow:hidden;}.ds-evidence-panel header{padding:17px 19px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border,#272b36);}.ds-evidence-panel h2{font-size:15px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.015em;margin:0;color:var(--foreground,#f3f4f6);}.ds-evidence-panel>div{min-height:322px;padding:52px 28px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-direction:column;text-align:center;}.ds-evidence-panel h3{font-size:15px;font-weight:550;margin:0;color:var(--foreground,#f3f4f6);}.ds-evidence-panel p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.9;max-width:33ch;margin:11px 0 0;color:var(--muted,#a8afbd);}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-evidence-panel>div{min-height:235px;padding:31px 20px;}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Evidence beside the next action",
    "overview": "AuthPilot is a focused developer workspace built from deep charcoal, restrained violet, compact navigation, and readable documentation. The user-supplied **AuthPilot OAuth Integration Flow.png** is the visual authority: its four panels become connected Explore, Research, Guide, and Library screens. This approved reference replaces the previous identity. Its example provider policies, verification badges, countdown, and account controls are not product evidence.\n\nThe interface balances a compact operating view for finding providers and following research with an open reading view for source-linked requirements. Violet identifies actions and selected states; evidence has its own labelled semantic colors. Flat surfaces and alignment provide structure. Actual source styles and components are authoritative when an earlier screenshot differs from the final code.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark by default, with an equivalent working light theme.",
      "One top navigation and separate connected screens.",
      "Restrained violet actions against charcoal surfaces and fine borders.",
      "Evidence labels and citations beside the claims they qualify.",
      "Actual research events and personal checklist progress with distinct meanings."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Named Evidence Rule.",
        "body": "Pair evidence color with its text label and icon; retain explicit uncertainty and attached citations.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Useful Violet Rule.",
        "body": "Reserve violet for actions, links, focus, selection, and actual progress; use semantic evidence colors for evidence.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Measure Rule.",
        "body": "Keep requirement claims at 15px with 1.8 line height inside the 75ch reading measure; collapse columns before shrinking claims.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Workspace Rule.",
        "body": "Keep resting content panels flat; reserve the shared ambient shadow for the mobile navigation dialog.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve charcoal/violet semantic roles and the equivalent light-theme overrides.",
      "**Do** keep evidence labels, source links, estimates, and explicit unknowns beside relevant claims.",
      "**Do** retain 15px/1.8 requirement text and collapse supporting columns on small screens.",
      "**Do** preserve visible focus, labelled controls, functional navigation, and reduced motion.",
      "**Do** derive guide counts, source lists, dates, and checklist progress from actual state.",
      "**Do** keep public OAuth distribution, optional directory listing, and workspace approval distinct in the guide presentation."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** restore a global sidebar or use the four-screen reference as a collage inside one page.",
      "**Don't** add neon glows, glass effects, heavy gradients, decorative analytics, pricing, or upgrade widgets.",
      "**Don't** label a whole guide Verified or setup verified because documentation was retrieved.",
      "**Don't** invent research percentages, countdowns, sources, events, or provider approval timelines.",
      "**Don't** add avatars, account controls, Shared with me, or collaborative progress without working features.",
      "**Don't** use untrusted remote provider images or text glyphs as icon substitutes."
    ]
  }
}
